{ Train as Black in the Polish Defense. }
1. e3 { White opens the bishop’s diagonal. } c5 { Black advances the c-pawn, clearing c7 for the queen. } 2. Ba6 { White offers the bishop on a6. } Nxa6 { Black’s knight captures on a6. This is the Polish Defense starting position. The next chapters cover White’s b4, d4, Qh5, Qf3, and Qg4. } *

